  },
  "lines": [
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Mia, how does my heart pump blood?",
      "board": {
        "type": "title",
        "left": {
          "icon": "img:Human_physiology/Servier/heart-front",
          "label": "Heart"
        },
        "right": {
          "icon": "🩸",
          "label": "Blood"
        },
        "mid": "?"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Great question, Leo! Today we're going on a big trip with your heart and your blood.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🗺️",
        "text": "A trip with your heart",
        "cue": "trip",
        "sub": "And your blood!",
        "sub_cue": "blood"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Will we find out why it goes thump-thump?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Yes! We'll meet your heart, follow your blood, hear the lub-dub, and find out why it speeds up.",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "What we'll find out",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": "Meet your heart",
            "icon": "❤️",
            "cue": "meet"
          },
          {
            "label": "Follow your blood",
            "icon": "🩸",
            "cue": "follow"
          },
          {
            "label": "Hear the lub-dub",
            "icon": "👂",
            "cue": "lub"
          },
          {
            "label": "Why it speeds up",
            "icon": "🏃",
            "cue": "speeds"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "So where is my heart, and how big is it?",
      "chapter": "Meet your heart"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Your heart sits in the middle of your chest, tipped a little to the left. It's about as big as your fist.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "img:Human_physiology/Servier/heart-front",
        "text": "Middle of your chest",
        "cue": "middle",
        "sub": "As big as your fist",
        "sub_cue": "fist"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "My fist is small! Is my heart small too?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Yes! Your heart grows as you grow. Make a fist, and that's about the size of your heart right now.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "✊",
        "text": "Make a fist!",
        "cue": "fist",
        "sub": "That's your heart's size",
        "sub_cue": "size"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Is it shaped like a love heart?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Not really! A real heart is shaped more like a big, lumpy strawberry. And it's made of strong muscle.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "img:Human_physiology/Servier/heart-front",
        "text": "A real heart",
        "cue": "real",
        "sub": "Strong muscle!",
        "sub_cue": "muscle"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Inside, your heart has four little rooms. Two rooms on top take blood in. Two rooms on the bottom pump it out.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "img:Human_physiology/Servier/heart-chambers-visible",
        "text": "Four little rooms",
        "cue": "four",
        "sub": "Top in, bottom out",
        "sub_cue": "top"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Four rooms? My heart is like a tiny house!",
      "punch": "house"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "A tiny house with a wall down the middle! The right side and the left side each have a different job.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🏠",
        "text": "A wall down the middle",
        "cue": "wall",
        "sub": "Two sides, two jobs",
        "sub_cue": "different"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "What are the two jobs?",
      "chapter": "Blood's big trip"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "The right side sends blood to your lungs. There, the blood picks up oxygen from the air you breathe in.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "img:Human_physiology/Servier/healthy-lung",
        "text": "Off to the lungs!",
        "cue": "lungs",
        "sub": "Pick up oxygen",
        "sub_cue": "oxygen"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "What's oxygen?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Oxygen is an invisible gas in the air. Every part of your body needs it to stay alive and make energy.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "💨",
        "text": "Oxygen is in the air",
        "cue": "oxygen",
        "sub": "Your body needs it",
        "sub_cue": "needs"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Then the blood goes back to your heart. The left side squeezes hard and pumps it to your head, your arms, your tummy and your toes!",
      "board": {
        "type": "body",
        "title": "Blood's big trip",
        "show": [
          "heart",
          "lungs"
        ],
        "flow": "blood",
        "cue": "squeezes",
        "labels": [
          {
            "text": "Head",
            "at": "head",
            "cue": "head"
          },
          {
            "text": "Arms",
            "at": "arm",
            "cue": "arms"
          },
          {
            "text": "Tummy",
            "at": "stomach",
            "cue": "tummy"
          },
          {
            "text": "Toes",
            "at": "foot",
            "cue": "toes"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "How does the blood get all the way to my toes?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Through tubes called blood vessels. They go everywhere in your body, like roads in a big city.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🛣️",
        "text": "Blood vessels",
        "cue": "vessels",
        "sub": "Like roads in a city",
        "sub_cue": "roads"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Arteries are big tubes that carry blood away from your heart. Veins are tubes that bring it back again.",
      "board": {
        "type": "compare",
        "left": {
          "label": "Arteries",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Big tubes",
              "icon": "🩸",
              "cue": "arteries"
            },
            {
              "text": "Away from heart",
              "icon": "➡️",
              "cue": "away"
            }
          ]
        },
        "right": {
          "label": "Veins",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Back to heart",
              "icon": "⬅️",
              "cue": "back"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "And the tiniest tubes are called capillaries. They're thinner than a hair! They pass oxygen to every part of you.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🧵",
        "text": "Capillaries: super tiny!",
        "cue": "capillaries",
        "sub": "Thinner than a hair",
        "sub_cue": "thinner"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Wait, my veins look blue. Is some of my blood blue?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Nope! Blood is always red. Veins only look blue because you see them through your skin.",
      "board": {
        "type": "checklist",
        "title": "Blood is...",
        "icon": "🩸",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Sometimes blue",
            "icon": "🔵",
            "cue": "nope",
            "ok": false
          },
          {
            "text": "Always red",
            "icon": "🔴",
            "cue": "red",
            "ok": true
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "And then the blood comes back to my heart?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Yes! Your body uses up the oxygen and makes waste air. The blood carries it back, and your lungs breathe it out.",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "Coming home",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": "Body uses oxygen",
            "icon": "💪",
            "cue": "uses"
          },
          {
            "label": "Blood carries waste air",
            "icon": "🩸",
            "cue": "carries"
          },
          {
            "label": "Lungs breathe it out",
            "icon": "🫁",
            "cue": "breathe"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "So your blood goes round and round: heart to lungs, back to heart, out to your body, and home again!",
      "board": {
        "type": "cycle",
        "title": "Round and round",
        "center": "🩸",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "❤️",
            "label": "Heart",
            "cue": "heart"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🫁",
            "label": "Lungs",
            "cue": "lungs"
          },
          {
            "icon": "💗",
            "label": "Back to heart",
            "cue": "back"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🧍",
            "label": "Your body",
            "cue": "body"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🏠",
            "label": "Home again",
            "cue": "home"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Round and round, like a race track!"
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Mia, what makes the lub-dub sound?",
      "chapter": "The lub-dub doors",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "👂",
        "text": "Lub-dub?",
        "cue": "lub"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Your heart has four little doors inside, called valves. They open to let blood through, then snap shut.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "img:Human_physiology/Servier/heart-valves",
        "text": "Four valves",
        "cue": "valves",
        "sub": "Open, then snap shut",
        "sub_cue": "open"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Why do they snap shut?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "So blood can only go one way! The doors stop it from sliding backwards, like a door that only opens one way.",
      "board": {
        "type": "compare",
        "left": {
          "label": "Open",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Blood flows on",
              "icon": "➡️",
              "cue": "one"
            }
          ]
        },
        "right": {
          "label": "Shut",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "No going back",
              "icon": "🚫",
              "cue": "backwards"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "When the valves close, they make the sound. Lub is one set of doors closing. Dub is the other set!",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "Lub-dub",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": "Lub: doors close",
            "icon": "🚪",
            "cue": "lub"
          },
          {
            "label": "Dub: more doors close",
            "icon": "🚪",
            "cue": "dub"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Can I hear my own heart?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Doctors use a listening tool called a stethoscope. You can also feel your heartbeat. Ask a grown-up to help you find it on your wrist or neck.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🩺",
        "text": "A stethoscope",
        "cue": "stethoscope",
        "sub": "Feel it on your wrist",
        "sub_cue": "wrist"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Each bump you feel is called your pulse. It's your blood being pushed along with every heartbeat.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "💓",
        "text": "That's your pulse!",
        "cue": "pulse",
        "sub": "One bump, one beat",
        "sub_cue": "every"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "When I run, my heart goes really fast. Why?",
      "chapter": "Fast and slow",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🏃",
        "text": "Why so fast?",
        "cue": "fast"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "When you run, your muscles work hard and need extra oxygen. So your heart beats faster to bring more blood to them.",
      "punch": "faster",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "Running!",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": "Muscles work hard",
            "icon": "img:Human_physiology/Servier/muscle-1",
            "cue": "muscles"
          },
          {
            "label": "Need more oxygen",
            "icon": "💨",
            "cue": "oxygen"
          },
          {
            "label": "Heart beats faster",
            "icon": "💓",
            "cue": "faster"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Who tells my heart to go faster?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Your brain does! It sends a message, and your heart speeds up. You don't even have to think about it.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "img:Human_physiology/Servier/brain-1",
        "text": "Your brain helps",
        "cue": "brain",
        "sub": "No thinking needed!",
        "sub_cue": "think"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "And your heart has its own tiny spark inside. It tells the heart when to squeeze, again and again, all day and all night.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "⚡",
        "text": "Its own tiny spark",
        "cue": "spark",
        "sub": "Squeeze, squeeze, squeeze!",
        "sub_cue": "squeeze"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "When does it go slow?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "When you play, it beats fast. When you rest or sleep, your body needs less oxygen, so your heart slows down.",
      "board": {
        "type": "compare",
        "left": {
          "label": "Playing",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Fast beats",
              "icon": "🏃",
              "cue": "play"
            }
          ]
        },
        "right": {
          "label": "Sleeping",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Slow beats",
              "icon": "😴",
              "cue": "sleep"
            },
            {
              "text": "Less oxygen",
              "icon": "💨",
              "cue": "less"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Wow. How many times does my heart beat?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "A grown-up's heart beats about a hundred thousand times every day! And a kid's heart beats even a bit faster.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🔢",
        "text": "About 100,000 a day!",
        "cue": "hundred",
        "sub": "Kids' hearts: faster!",
        "sub_cue": "kid"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "How can I keep my heart strong?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Run, jump and play every day! Eat lots of fruit and veggies, drink water, and get good sleep.",
      "board": {
        "type": "checklist",
        "title": "Strong heart",
        "icon": "❤️",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Run, jump and play",
            "icon": "🏃",
            "cue": "run",
            "ok": true
          },
          {
            "text": "Fruit and veggies",
            "icon": "🍎",
            "cue": "fruit",
            "ok": true
          },
          {
            "text": "Drink water",
            "icon": "💧",
            "cue": "drink",
            "ok": true
          },
          {
            "text": "Good sleep",
            "icon": "😴",
            "cue": "sleep",
            "ok": true
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Quiz time, Leo! Question one: what is your heart made of? Think...",
      "chapter": "Quiz time",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "❓",
        "text": "What is your heart made of?",
        "cue": "made"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Muscle! A strong muscle about the size of my fist.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "img:Human_physiology/Servier/heart-front",
        "text": "Muscle!",
        "cue": "muscle",
        "sub": "As big as your fist",
        "sub_cue": "fist"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Right! Question two: what do the valves do? Think...",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "❓",
        "text": "What do valves do?",
        "cue": "valves"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "They're little doors that keep blood going one way. Lub-dub!",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "img:Human_physiology/Servier/heart-valves",
        "text": "Doors: one way only",
        "cue": "doors",
        "sub": "Lub-dub!",
        "sub_cue": "lub"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Yes! Last one: where does blood go to pick up oxygen? Think...",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "❓",
        "text": "Where does blood get oxygen?",
        "cue": "oxygen"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "To the lungs!",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "img:Human_physiology/Servier/healthy-lung",
        "text": "The lungs!",
        "cue": "lungs"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "You got them all! Let's sum it all up.",
      "chapter": "Recap",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🏆",
        "text": "You got them all!",
        "cue": "got"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "My heart is a muscle that squeezes. It sends blood to my lungs, then all around me. Valves keep it going one way, and it speeds up when I play!",
      "board": {
        "type": "summary",
        "rows": [
          {
            "text": "A squeezing muscle",
            "icon": "💪",
            "cue": "muscle"
          },
          {
            "text": "To lungs, then body",
            "icon": "🫁",
            "cue": "lungs"
          },
          {
            "text": "Valves: one way",
            "icon": "🚪",
            "cue": "valves"
          },
          {
            "text": "Faster when you play",
            "icon": "🏃",
            "cue": "speeds"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Every day and every night, even while you sleep! Ask a grown-up to subscribe to The Curio Kids Club for more wonders, and share this with a friend! And next time someone asks... how does my heart pump blood?"
    }
  ]
}